WHY HOAs NEED A PUBLIC ADJUSTER

Managing a community means being responsible for a wide range of insured assets: roofs, common areas, pools, clubhouses, fencing, landscaping, and more. When a hurricane, windstorm, fire, or other covered event occurs, the damage can be extensive and complex—and insurance companies often under-value or underpay HOA claims.

A Licensed Public Adjuster works exclusively on behalf of the policyholder—in this case, your HOA—not the insurance carrier. We ensure that:

  • Every damaged item is properly documented and accounted for.
  • Your policy is thoroughly reviewed for all applicable coverage.
  • Your claim is prepared, submitted, and negotiated to maximize the settlement.
  • Your board and community members are kept informed throughout the process.
  • Deadlines and compliance requirements are met to protect your claim.

OUR HOA SERVICES

  ✔ Pre-Disaster Policy Review – Know your coverage BEFORE you need it.
  ✔ Post-Loss Claim Management – We handle everything from documentation to settlement.
  ✔ Supplemental Claims – Already settled? We can re-open and supplement under-paid claims.
  ✔ Board & Resident Education – We offer free informational sessions for HOA boards and residents.
  ✔ Emergency Response Coordination – We coordinate quickly after a disaster to protect your property and claim.

HOW WE ARE PAID

Our fee is a percentage of the final insurance settlement. There is no upfront cost and no fee if we do not recover funds for your community.

